@startuml msm-operations
' liblevenshtein — the three Move-Split-Merge (MSM) edit operations on a time series.
' MSM transforms one numeric series into another using only these three moves; the
' metric is the minimum total cost over all such transformations.
' Color legend (time-series / MSM concept):
'   container  #B2DFDB  (deep-teal)   = the MSM metric / operation set
'   children   #E0F2F1  (teal tint)   = the individual operations
'   border     #00695C  (deep teal)   = all time-series borders & arrows
' Cost model (c = the constant split/merge cost from MsmConfig):
'   Move  changes one value in place                 → cost = |xᵢ − y|
'   Split duplicates one value into two copies        → cost = c + |xᵢ − y|
'   Merge collapses two equal adjacent values into one → cost = c + |xᵢ − xⱼ|
skinparam backgroundColor #FFFFFF
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "DejaVu Sans"
skinparam rectangle {
  RoundCorner 14
  BorderColor #455A64
  FontColor #102027
}
skinparam ArrowColor #37474F
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

title MSM metric — edit a series with Move / Split / Merge

rectangle "MSM metric: edit a series with Move / Split / Merge" as title #B2DFDB {
  rectangle "Move — change a value  <latex>x_{i}</latex> → y\n(cost = <latex>\vert x_{i} - y\vert</latex>)" as move #E0F2F1
  rectangle "Split — one value → two copies\n(cost = c + <latex>\vert x_{i} - y\vert</latex>)" as split #E0F2F1
  rectangle "Merge — two adjacent values → one\n(cost = c + <latex>\vert x_{i} - x_{j}\vert</latex>)" as merge #E0F2F1
}

move  -[#00695C]right-> split
split -[#00695C]right-> merge

note bottom of title
  MSM distance = minimum total cost over all
  Move / Split / Merge transformations of X into Y.
  Stefan, Athitsos & Das, "The Move-Split-Merge
  Metric for Time Series", IEEE TKDE 25(6):1425–1438, 2013.
  DOI 10.1109/TKDE.2012.88
end note

@enduml
